The semantic search stage embeds a model in the binary: the files under
assets/model/. It is derived from

sentence-transformers/static-similarity-mrl-multilingual-v1
https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/static-similarity-mrl-multilingual-v1

which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Leteo changed it: the embedding
table is cut to its first 256 dimensions, quantised to 8-bit integers, and the
tokenizer vocabulary and the table rows are pruned to the pieces used by the
languages Leteo supports. tools/semantic/ rebuilds those files from the
original, and tools/semantic/checksums.json records what each one hashes to.

The model is compiled into the leteo binary, so every copy of the binary carries
it. The full text of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is in
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt, which ships with the source and in the crate.

Rust dependency notices and source links are generated in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.html from Cargo.lock. Leteo does not modify the MPL-2.0
dependency sources distributed through crates.io.
